ng"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 6797, "total_tokens": 6797}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nCloud Foundry, a key environment for SAP's technology components, has seen significant updates in 2025. These updates include the introduction of new use cases in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition, improvements in the scheduling module of the Availability Service, and the addition of new resource tags for Job Execution and Task Execution Service Events. These changes aim to enhance the reliability and performance of Cloud Foundry, supporting SAP's operational stability and innovation. [Data: Sources (69, 193), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 23), (2025, 09, 23))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime, another critical environment for SAP's technology components, has also seen significant updates in 2025. These updates include the introduction of new features, bug fixes, and changes in the Istio module, such as the support for installation with Istio images injected into the installer from environment variables. These changes aim to enhance the reliability and performance of Kyma Runtime, supporting SAP's operational stability and innovation. [Data: Sources (70, 407), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 22), (2025, 08, 11))]\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Updates\n\nDecentralized Identity Verification, a key component of SAP's technology, has seen significant updates in 2025. These updates include the introduction of automated matching of credentials, improvement of the company identity status check, and retrieval of shared verifiable presentation using access token. These changes aim to enhance the reliability and performance of Decentralized Identity Verification, supporting SAP's operational stability and innovation. [Data: Sources (322, 323, 324), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 08, 12))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP Technology Overview as of July 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key components and services within the Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP technology ecosystem, highlighting their relationships and significant updates as of July 2025. The information is relevant to the company's operations and strategic planning.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Foundry has undergone significant updates and enhancements in 2025, including the introduction of new features and services. These updates aim to improve the reliability, performance, and scalability of the platform, supporting the company's digital transformation and innovation efforts. [Data: Sources (193, 402, 405), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 24))]\n\n## SAP BTP Updates and Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP has also seen significant updates and enhancements in 2025, including the introduction of new features and services. These updates aim to improve the integration, security, and scalability of the platform, supporting the company's digital transformation and innovation efforts. [Data: Sources (28, 403, 406), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 24))]\n\n## Interoperability and Integration\n\nThe updates and enhancements in Cloud Foundry and SAP BTP have improved interoperability and integration between the two platforms, enabling seamless communication and data exchange. This has significant implications for the company's digital transformation and innovation efforts, enabling the creation of new business models and revenue streams. [Data: Sources (193, 402, 405), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 01), (2025, 07, 24))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance the overall user experience and improve operational efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2025.\n\n## Joule and OAuth2ClientCredentials Authentication\n\nThe document grounding capability now supports OAuth2ClientCredentials authentication when you create a destination configuration in the SAP BTP cockpit. This update enhances the overall security and reliability of SAP's technology infrastructure. Effective authentication measures not only prevent unauthorized access but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (318, 1631), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 13), (2025, 01, 15))]\n\n## Istio Module Update\n\nThe Istio module has been updated to version 1.12.0, allowing users to configure Istio Egress Gateway in the Istio custom resource. This update enables users to specify exit points from the Istio service mesh and apply a range of Istio features, like monitoring and routing policies, to their outbound traffic. [Data: Sources (1632), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 30), (2025, 01, 13))]\n\n## Zero Maintenance Downtime\n\nThe weekly maintenance windows have been eliminated, and major upgrade windows have been shortened from 8 hours to 4 hours, and start times aligned with BTP and HANA Cloud. This update enhances the overall user experience and improves operational efficiency. Effective maintenance strategies not only prevent downtime but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1630, 1633, 1634), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 13), (2025, 01, 17))]", "# Cloud Foundry and SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key updates and changes within the Cloud Foundry and SAP technology ecosystem, highlighting the importance of these updates in enhancing user experience, improving operational efficiency, and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. The information is relevant to the technology landscape as of 2025.\n\n## Enhanced User Experience through Document Management Service Updates\n\nThe Document Management Service has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of the changeLogDuration parameter and the enhancement of thumbnail generation for document updates. These updates aim to improve user experience by reducing errors related to outdated tokens and providing a visual representation of the latest content. The updates also enhance the overall usability of the Document Management Service, making it easier for users to manage documents and access historical change log data. [Data: Sources (241, 238), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 24), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Improved Onboarding for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\n\nThe SAP Task Center has introduced an improved onboarding process for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition with the all-tasks service plan. This update automates the process of enabling the destination, eliminating the need for an additional ticket. The improved onboarding process enhances the user experience and reduces the administrative burden associated with setting up SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition. [Data: Source (1336), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 02, 25))]\n\n## Enhanced Security through Identity Provisioning Updates\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component has introduced documentation for troubleshooting entity deletion issues. This update aims to improve the overall security and stability of the technology ecosystem by providing users with the necessary tools to resolve common issues related to entity deletion. The update also enhances the user experience by providing clear guidance on troubleshooting entity deletion issues. [Data: Source (240), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 02, 25))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships, core attributes, and connections. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2024.\n\n## Generative AI Hub Deprecation\n\nThe Generative AI hub, a key component of SAP's AI strategy, has been deprecated as of September 1, 2024. Users are advised to choose another model. This change is part of SAP's efforts to maintain a cutting-edge AI infrastructure and ensure seamless user experience. [Data: Sources (476, 2332), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 01), (2024, 09, 01))]\n\n## SAP UI Theme Designer Updates\n\nThe SAP UI Theme Designer has undergone significant updates, including the deprecation of the Belize theme as a base for new themes. Users are recommended to migrate their themes to Horizon or Quartz themes. This change is part of SAP's efforts to maintain a modern and user-friendly UI experience. [Data: Sources (2336, 1337), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 28), (2025, 02, 24))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced several updates, including the ability to create scheduled triggers to start processes. This feature is part of SAP's efforts to enhance process automation and improve user experience. [Data: Sources (2335, 2338), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 29), (2025, 02, 25))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's technology landscape, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning\n\nCloud Identity Services and Identity Provisioning are two critical components of SAP's technology landscape. Cloud Identity Services provides identity authentication, while Identity Provisioning supports the SAP Ariba Category Management connector. Their collaboration ensures seamless user experiences and efficient identity management. [Data: Sources (731, 545), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 06, 20))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell and Pricing Service\n\nEdge Integration Cell and Pricing Service are two key components that support SAP's operations. Edge Integration Cell enables outgoing connections through a proxy, while Pricing Service corrects issues with engine traces. Their updates ensure efficient data processing and accurate pricing. [Data: Sources (2755, 3520), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 09), (2024, 06, 20))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps and SAP Datasphere\n\nSAP Build Apps and SAP Datasphere are two critical components that support SAP's innovation and customer satisfaction. SAP Build Apps provides web and mobile applications, while SAP Datasphere offers data cataloging, integration, and modeling. Their updates ensure efficient data management and innovative applications. [Data: Sources (2744, 3518), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 13))]", "# Cloud Identity Services Overview as of August 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of Cloud Identity Services, focusing on key components, their operational scope, and recent updates. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations around August 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at the company play a pivotal role in managing user identities, authentication, and authorization. Their proactive approach helps safeguard the company against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (1, 2), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 01), (2024, 08, 20))]\n\n## Recent Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Identity Services have undergone several updates and enhancements in August 2024, including changes to condition and skip operations, support for new email validation, and improvements to user management. These updates aim to enhance the security, efficiency, and compliance of the company's technology operations. [Data: Sources (3, 4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 01), (2024, 08, 20))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Identity Management\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and other departments is essential for holistic identity management and ensuring that security measures are aligned with regulatory requirements. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in maintaining the company's technology operations and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (7, 8), Date_Range ((2024, 08, 01), (2024, 08, 20))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of May 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and security. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations around May 2024.\n\n## SAP Java Buildpack Updates\n\nThe SAP Java Buildpack at SAP has been updated from version 2.7.0 to 2.9.0, incorporating various improvements and bug fixes. This update enhances the build process, ensuring smoother and more efficient deployment of SAP applications. The update also includes the latest versions of SapMachine, Apache Tomcat, and other dependencies, ensuring compatibility and security. This proactive approach to buildpack updates demonstrates SAP's commitment to maintaining a stable and secure development environment. [Data: Sources (2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 22), (2024, 05, 30))]\n\n## Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK Enhancements\n\nThe Microsoft 365 Cloud SDK at SAP has been enhanced with various Microsoft Teams activities, including the creation of chats, retrieval of chat lists, sending of chat messages, and retrieval of user availability. This update enables developers to leverage the full potential of Microsoft Teams, streamlining collaboration and communication within SAP's technology ecosystem. The addition of these activities underscores SAP's commitment to providing a comprehensive and user-friendly development experience. [Data: Sources (1, 4), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 29), (2024, 05, 29))]\n\n## Custom Security Header for SAPUI5\n\nDue to an update in the Strict Tracking Prevention policy in Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge, certain SAPUI5 elements were being blocked, preventing site loading. To address this issue, a new SAPUI5 domain has been made available, allowing full site loading. This update ensures that SAPUI5 applications continue to function seamlessly, even with the latest browser updates. The recommended action to add the new SAPUI5 URL to custom security headers underscores SAP's commitment to maintaining a secure and stable development environment. [Data: Source (6), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 28), (2024, 05, 28))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the community's operations as of 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Component Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP community has seen significant updates across various components, including SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration, SAP Document AI, and SAP Task Center. These updates have improved the community's ability to manage financial risks, enhance data quality, and streamline task management. Effective component updates not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the community's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2851, 2853, 2854), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 29), (2024, 11, 13))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between various departments within the SAP BTP community, such as Risk Management and Legal Compliance, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the community's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2851, 2853, 2854), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 29), (2024, 11, 13))]\n\n## SAP BTP Component Relationships\n\nThe SAP BTP community consists of various components, including SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration, SAP Document AI, and SAP Task Center. These components interact with each other to provide a comprehensive solution for managing financial risks, enhancing data quality, and streamlining task management. Effective component relationships not only prevent operational anomalies but also support the community's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2851, 2853, 2854), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 29), (2024, 11, 13))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into key updates and changes within SAP's technology framework, highlighting the importance of these updates in maintaining the company's operational stability and compliance with evolving market regulations. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Improved Protection Against Cross-Site Request Forgery\n\nSAP has improved protection against Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) in SAP Build Process Automation. New subscriptions automatically have CSRF protection enforced, and for any modifying PUT/POST/DELETE calls, CSRF protection became mandatory. This update is crucial in safeguarding SAP's systems against potential security threats and ensuring continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective security measures not only prevent security breaches but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (135, 200), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 24), (2024, 05, 28))]\n\n## Enhanced User Experience with Preferences\n\nSAP has introduced a new feature in SAP Build Process Automation, allowing users to access key user details such as Name, Email, Identity Provider, Role Collections, and User Groups under a single option in the Preferences section. This update facilitates easier access to user details, enhancing the overall user experience and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (2857, 200), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 24), (2024, 05, 28))]\n\n## Google's Third-Party Cookies Deprecation\n\nGoogle plans to phase out support for third-party cookies, and SAP has provided guidance on how to prepare for this change. The company recommends participating in the third-party deprecation trial and applying the necessary tokens for Kyma workloads. This update is crucial in ensuring SAP's systems remain compliant with evolving market regulations and maintaining the company's operational integrity. [Data: Sources (2860, 200), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 23), (2024, 05, 28))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of November 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting the importance of these changes in maintaining the company's operational stability and technological advancements. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around November 2023.\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nThe Kyma Runtime has undergone significant updates, including the release of the API Gateway module, which provides functionalities for exposing and securing APIs. Additionally, the Telemetry module has been updated to version 1.3.0, bringing improvements to logs and traces. These updates are crucial for maintaining the company's technological advancements and operational stability. [Data: Sources (256, 201, 201), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 10), (2023, 11, 20))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has introduced several updates, including the restriction of the refresh token flow of OIDC protocol to the validity of the web session. This change ensures that refresh tokens expire with the user session, unless the offline_access scope is added. Additionally, the Implicit grant type is disabled by default for new applications. These updates are essential for maintaining the company's security and operational stability. [Data: Sources (380, 708), Date_Range ((2023, 08, 16), (2023, 11, 22))]\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Updates\n\nContinuous Integration & Delivery has introduced several updates, including automatic login with WebdriverIO tests, failing jobs in case of an invalid package.json file, and information about credential usage. These updates are crucial for maintaining the company's operational stability and technological advancements. [Data: Sources (708, 132), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 23), (2023, 10, 23))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, focusing on key components and their interactions within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Continuous Integration & Delivery Operational Scope\n\nThe Continuous Integration & Delivery (CID) component at SAP Cloud Services plays a pivotal role in streamlining software development and deployment processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2023, helps safeguard SAP Cloud Services against potential technical pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective CID not only prevents software anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (482, 264), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 19), (2024, 09, 11))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services component ensures that all SAP Cloud Services operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on identity management and access control, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP Cloud Services' reputation and operational legality, especially in managing user identities and access permissions. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (2293), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 10), (2024, 09, 11))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Continuous Integration & Delivery and Cloud Identity Services components, established in 2024, ensures that software development and deployment strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider technical risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating software development with identity management strategies at SAP Cloud Services. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (2294, 2295), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 10), (2024, 09, 11))]", "# SAP Technology and Finance Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and finance, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Technology Operational Scope\n\nThe Technology Department at SAP plays a pivotal role in identifying, assessing, and mitigating financial risks. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (532, 533), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 05))]\n\n## Finance and Credit Integration\n\nThe Finance Department ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on credit integration and risk management, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (533), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 05))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Technology and Finance Departments, established in 2024, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (532, 533), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 02, 05))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold technological standards and manage software updates effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment Updates\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment at SAP has seen significant updates in 2024, with new features and improvements being added regularly. This includes the introduction of new services, such as the Event Connectivity service plan, and the enhancement of existing services, such as the Cloud Identity Services. These updates have improved the overall performance and reliability of the Cloud Foundry environment, making it a more attractive option for SAP customers. [Data: Sources (602, 603), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 05, 23))]\n\n## ABAP Environment Updates\n\nThe ABAP Environment at SAP has also seen significant updates in 2024, with new features and improvements being added regularly. This includes the introduction of new tools, such as the ABAP Development Tools for Eclipse, and the enhancement of existing tools, such as the ABAP Runtime Error viewer. These updates have improved the overall performance and reliability of the ABAP Environment, making it a more attractive option for SAP customers. [Data: Sources (2891, 2892), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 17), (2024, 05, 17))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell Updates\n\nThe Edge Integration Cell at SAP has seen significant updates in 2025, with new features and improvements being added regularly. This includes the introduction of new services, such as the RFC Sender adapter, and the enhancement of existing services, such as the Edge Integration Cell runtime. These updates have improved the overall performance and reliability of the Edge Integration Cell, making it a more attractive option for SAP customers. [Data: Sources (401, 911), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 11), (2025, 05, 11))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and compliance. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services at SAP have undergone significant updates, including the removal of the read applications permission from the MANAGE_USERS policy, the introduction of central store logs, and the implementation of new conditional functions. These updates aim to enhance the security and compliance of SAP's cloud identity services, ensuring that users have the necessary permissions and that logs are properly stored and monitored. Effective cloud identity services are crucial for maintaining the integrity of SAP's cloud-based operations and ensuring that users have the necessary access to resources. The updates also demonstrate SAP's commitment to staying up-to-date with the latest security and compliance standards, which is essential for maintaining the trust of its customers and partners. [Data: Sources (3, 4, 5), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 11), (2025, 02, 12))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps Updates\n\nSAP Build Apps has undergone several updates, including the removal of the option to upload the iOS distribution certificate when creating iOS build configurations, the introduction of a new context menu, and the ability to generate app pages using AI. These updates aim to enhance the governance and security of SAP Build Apps, ensuring that users have the necessary permissions and that the development process is streamlined. Effective governance and security are crucial for maintaining the integrity of SAP's cloud-based operations and ensuring that users have the necessary access to resources. The updates also demonstrate SAP's commitment to staying up-to-date with the latest security and compliance standards, which is essential for maintaining the trust of its customers and partners. [Data: Sources (6, 7, 8), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone has undergone several updates, including the introduction of Identity Authentication as the default authentication mechanism for new subscriptions, the ability to retrieve user profile information from the SCIM API, and the enhancement of the wizard. These updates aim to enhance the security and compliance of SAP Build Work Zone, ensuring that users have the necessary permissions and that the development process is streamlined. Effective security and compliance are crucial for maintaining the integrity of SAP's cloud-based operations and ensuring that users have the necessary access to resources. The updates also demonstrate SAP's commitment to staying up-to-date with the latest security and compliance standards, which is essential for maintaining the trust of its customers and partners. [Data: Sources (9, 10, 11), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 20), (2025, 03, 20))]", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into key SAP technology updates, highlighting how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and maintain regulatory standards. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Alert Notification Service Updates\n\nThe SAP Alert Notification Service has been updated to integrate with OpenSearch Enhanced with OpenSearch Dashboards [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]. This integration enables users to find information about the integration of SAP Alert Notification service with OpenSearch. The update is part of SAP's efforts to enhance its technology offerings and improve user experience. [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nSAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime has been updated from 43.6.0 to 44.0.0 [Data: Source (2013), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 21), (2024, 10, 31))]. This update includes various enhancements, such as improved performance and security features. The update is part of SAP's efforts to maintain its technology infrastructure and ensure operational stability. [Data: Source (2013), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 21), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition has been updated with various features, including App Finder Enhancements [Data: Sources (2014, 2020), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))], Content Export Enhancements [Data: Source (2015), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))], and Create a Wizard Based on a SAP Build Process Automation Guided Process [Data: Source (2016), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]. These updates are part of SAP's efforts to enhance its technology offerings and improve user experience. [Data: Sources (2014, 2020), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]\n\n## Deprecation of the Container-Based Applications Pipeline\n\nThe Container-Based Applications pipeline has been deprecated and will be removed from the service on December 31st, 2024 [Data: Source (1686), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 31), (2024, 12, 31))]. Existing jobs will continue to function until this date. SAP recommends using the Kyma Runtime pipeline instead. [Data: Source (1686), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 31), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## New Google Cloud Region for SAP Document AI\n\nSAP Document AI is now available in the Google Cloud region ap30 - Australia (Sydney) [Data: Source (1687), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 30), (2024, 12, 30))]. This update is part of SAP's efforts to expand its technology offerings and improve user experience. [Data: Source (1687), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 30), (2024, 12, 30))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_35bd8751c6c956dd8d0335b7c64d5cdc368951b1409c414c805376412f5fcf15_v2"}